    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "DMARDs, esp MTX and bio (eg, etanercept, anakinra, canakinumab, tocilizumab, abatacept), have chged JIA tx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "MTX:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " useful for oligoarticular, psoriatic and polyarticular JIA; monitor for bone marrow depression and hepatotoxicity (CBC, AST, ALT, albumin)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "TNF inhibitors (etanercept, adalimumab, infliximab) if MTX fails or ↑risk of poor outcome."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "IL-1 inhibitors anakinra and canakinumab: esp effective for systemic JIA; tocilizumab (IL-6 receptor antagonist): systemic and polyarticular JIA."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
